<title>SWEDEN: Atlas Copco maintains positive forecast.</title>
<headline>Atlas Copco maintains positive forecast.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish industrial engineering group Atlas Copco said on Thursday it maintained its previously published forecast of a better full-year profit for 1996 than 1995.  </p>
<p>&quot;The previous forecast for 1996 for an improved result compared with the previous year is maintained,&quot; Atlas Copco said in announcing a nine-month profit after financial items of 2.23 billion crowns, a nine percent increase over the 1995 period.</p>
<p>Atlas said demand was seen as largely unchanged in the immediate future.</p>
<p>-- Simon Haydon, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1004</p>
